WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
In India, about 90 per cent of the
fresh water taken goes to agriculture.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.310
In the UK, it's almost the reverse:
about 74 per cent goes to homes.

3
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.210
Farms take about 14.

4
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.230
Worldwide, about 71 per
cent goes to agriculture.

5
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.130
Same three uses, opposite patterns.

6
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.390
Why the difference?

7
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.890
Do British homes simply waste more?

8
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.070
In this mission, you'll compare how richer
and poorer countries share out their

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.570
water, using real data.

10
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.630
Then you'll investigate three
problems with water supply,

11
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.630
from untreated water to failed rains.

12
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.710
Your mission: explain why India's
farms take most of its water,

13
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.730
while British homes take most of the UK's.
